WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.318
Default credentials, sample accounts, and vendor defaults are common attack targets.

2
00:00:05.318 --> 00:00:14.597
Any default identity, password, token, or administrative path should be removed, changed, or tightly controlled before production use.

3
00:00:14.597 --> 00:00:22.849
Open cloud storage and permissive access policies can expose sensitive records, exports, backups, logs, or artifacts.

4
00:00:22.849 --> 00:00:26.810
Cloud configuration must be treated as part of application security.

5
00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:29.504
Excessive services increase attack surface.

6
00:00:29.504 --> 00:00:38.404
Every enabled service, plugin, port, feature flag, debug endpoint, and administrative function should have a documented purpose and owner.

7
00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:47.843
Insecure defaults and debug interfaces may reveal stack traces, paths, secrets, environment details, and internal architecture.

8
00:00:47.843 --> 00:00:52.962
Diagnostic information belongs in protected logs, not public responses.

9
00:00:52.962 --> 00:00:58.509
Use hardened baselines for applications, systems, containers, and cloud services.

10
00:00:58.509 --> 00:01:02.471
Manage configuration through reviewed and repeatable processes.

11
00:01:02.471 --> 00:01:07.170
Apply least functionality by disabling unnecessary services and features.

12
